WEBVTT

00:03.809 --> 00:05.709
I had a great dream last night.

00:05.877 --> 00:07.208
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:07.379 --> 00:11.839
I dreamed I got locked in a house made of
doughnuts and I had to eat my way out.

00:12.818 --> 00:18.586
Interesting. I had a similar dream,
only no house and no doughnuts.

00:19.624 --> 00:20.648
- Morning.
Morning.

00:20.826 --> 00:21.952
Morning.

00:22.127 --> 00:24.823
So, uh, how'd everybody sleep?

00:26.832 --> 00:28.823
Uncle Charlie and
I both had dreams about eating.

00:29.000 --> 00:31.833
Mine was with doughnuts,
his was something dirty.

00:32.704 --> 00:33.966
He's just guessing.

00:35.107 --> 00:37.007
Good guess.

00:37.442 --> 00:39.273
And, yes, Alan, we see your earring.

00:40.746 --> 00:41.770
Pretty cool, right?

00:41.947 --> 00:45.781
Yeah, if you're going to a Wham! Concert
with Molly Ringwald.

00:47.919 --> 00:49.648
- I think it's cool.
- Thank you, Jake.

00:49.821 --> 00:51.584
- Can I get my ear pierced?
- No.

00:51.923 --> 00:55.359
- Why not?
- You can't keep the holes you have clean.

00:56.261 --> 00:57.694
And you're too young.

00:57.863 --> 01:01.128
Wait till you're old, desperate
and living in your brother's house.

01:01.399 --> 01:05.267
You can mock me all you want, but there's
a certain lady who thinks it's darn sexy.

01:05.437 --> 01:08.235
First of all,
I don't need permission to mock you.

01:08.406 --> 01:12.433
But more importantly, you let some broad
talk you into piercing your ear?

01:12.744 --> 01:16.373
Actually,
my ear wasrt her first choice to pierce.

01:17.783 --> 01:19.045
What else can you pierce?

01:21.953 --> 01:23.284
BoTH:
Nothing.

01:23.822 --> 01:26.620
Fine, don't tell me. I'll Google it.

01:27.325 --> 01:30.556
Don't worry. He can't spell pierce.

01:30.862 --> 01:33.023
He can't spell Google.

01:33.865 --> 01:36.959
So who's Princess Poke-a-Hole?

01:37.135 --> 01:40.127
Oh, just a nice young woman
with a sewing needle and a potato.

01:40.739 --> 01:41.797
A potato?

01:41.973 --> 01:44.874
Yeah. She put it behind my lobe,
sort of like a pincushion.

01:45.043 --> 01:47.477
Oh. So you're a moron.

01:48.013 --> 01:50.140
It's perfectly safe.
She sterilized the needle.

01:50.315 --> 01:53.045
- How?
- With alcohol.

01:55.086 --> 01:56.883
Okay, Kahlûa.

01:57.789 --> 02:01.020
Well, I guess I owe morons an apology.

02:01.927 --> 02:03.758
You do know that's the gay ear.

02:09.167 --> 02:10.429
What?

02:11.203 --> 02:14.104
Left ear says,
"I'm a hipster from the disco era. "

02:14.272 --> 02:17.173
Right ear says, "Let's disco. "

02:21.246 --> 02:22.543
No, no, that can't be right.

02:22.714 --> 02:24.181
Okay, don't believe me.

02:25.417 --> 02:28.909
Hey, look who's finally out of the closet.

02:50.408 --> 02:51.773
- Berta?
- Yeah?

02:51.943 --> 02:54.912
- What are you doing?
- Making your bed.

02:55.714 --> 02:57.409
Well, I'd like to take a nap.

02:57.749 --> 03:00.582
Hop in. You can spoon me,
but it ends there.

03:02.320 --> 03:05.517
- Are you sick?
- Yeah, I'm sick.

03:05.690 --> 03:08.488
I'm sick of staying up all night
with a screaming baby...

03:08.660 --> 03:12.619
...while my daughter's out trolling the
waterfront for the father of her next one.

03:13.265 --> 03:14.755
Whoa, that's rough.

03:15.066 --> 03:17.694
Oh, don't feign interest in my life,
Charlie.

03:18.503 --> 03:23.463
Sorry, I... I see a woman in my bed,
I instinctively start lying.

03:24.209 --> 03:26.109
Close the door on your way out.

03:26.878 --> 03:28.436
Okay.

03:33.518 --> 03:36.885
No. No, this is ridiculous.

03:37.055 --> 03:38.079
- Berta...
Get out.

03:38.256 --> 03:40.053
Sleep tight.

03:44.696 --> 03:46.061
Hello? Ow!

03:46.231 --> 03:47.562
Ooh...

03:47.732 --> 03:49.427
Uh, hello?

03:49.601 --> 03:53.401
Oh. Oh, hi.
Uh, no, no, it's just a little tender.

03:53.571 --> 03:55.471
I'm glad you called. I missed you too.

03:56.274 --> 03:58.708
Yeah, yeah, last night was fun. Ha, ha.

03:59.110 --> 04:00.737
You won't believe who's in my bed.

04:01.513 --> 04:02.673
Hang on.

04:02.847 --> 04:04.712
I never do...

04:05.684 --> 04:07.618
...but I'm on the phone right now.

04:07.786 --> 04:09.515
Ow! Aah.

04:09.688 --> 04:10.712
Damn it.

04:10.889 --> 04:12.322
Uh, listen, how about tonight?

04:12.891 --> 04:15.189
Oh, great, great. The usual place?

04:15.360 --> 04:16.520
I will see you then.

04:16.695 --> 04:18.560
Okay. Bye-bye.

04:19.597 --> 04:21.087
Berta's in my bed.

04:22.133 --> 04:23.361
Really?

04:23.535 --> 04:25.560
Couldrt you just
pay her in cash this week?

04:28.173 --> 04:29.197
Ow!

04:30.809 --> 04:32.834
There are some things
we don't joke about.

04:34.646 --> 04:38.082
Okay, so why is Berta in your bed?

04:38.516 --> 04:41.212
Apparently, her daughter's
been out partying every night...

04:41.386 --> 04:43.251
...and Berta's been stuck with the baby.
- Oh.

04:43.421 --> 04:44.513
That's gotta be rough.

04:45.657 --> 04:48.182
Don't feign interest in her life, Alan.

04:48.893 --> 04:51.726
Sorry. Oh, hey, hey, listen,
can you watch Jake tonight?

04:51.896 --> 04:56.128
Why, you wanna see if your new lady friend
can infect other parts of your body?

04:56.301 --> 04:59.464
It's not infected. A certain amount
of swelling is perfectly normal.

04:59.637 --> 05:02.265
Where'd it say that, Alan,
on the potato?

05:06.478 --> 05:08.537
You at least gonna tell me
who this woman is?

05:08.713 --> 05:10.647
It's nobody you know.

05:11.116 --> 05:13.243
Oh. So I know her.

05:14.519 --> 05:17.113
- I didn't say that.
- You didn't have to.

05:17.489 --> 05:20.890
Now, let's see. Who do I know that
you'd like to keep a secret?

05:21.059 --> 05:23.323
- You're wasting your time.
- One of your ex-wives?

05:23.495 --> 05:26.055
- Ha, ha.
- Rose? Berta's daughter?

05:26.231 --> 05:28.665
Berta's daughter? Ha-ha-ha.

05:30.535 --> 05:32.833
No, don't... Don't be ridiculous.

05:33.004 --> 05:34.232
Ha-ha-ha.

05:37.609 --> 05:39.702
That's rich. Ha, ha.

05:45.950 --> 05:47.850
I'm tired. Shouldrt I be in bed?

05:48.153 --> 05:49.620
Shut up and deal.

05:50.255 --> 05:52.519
Look, I'll give you back the money I won.

05:52.690 --> 05:55.352
You didn't win it till we stop playing.
Now deal.

05:58.296 --> 06:00.787
- What's he doing up?
- Not now, Alan.

06:00.965 --> 06:02.660
I'm all in.

06:03.435 --> 06:05.426
- Jake, bed.
- Hold on, Dad.

06:05.603 --> 06:07.366
Call you. Pocket aces.

06:08.306 --> 06:10.706
- What do you got?
- You heard your father, go to bed.

06:12.610 --> 06:14.339
Been betting on garbage all night.

06:16.314 --> 06:18.179
You let a 12-year-old beat you at poker?

06:18.917 --> 06:20.009
He's 12 and a half.

06:22.353 --> 06:24.583
What's going on with your ear, Dumbo?

06:24.856 --> 06:27.154
It's just a little swelling. It's normal.

06:28.193 --> 06:32.129
Better pierce the other one. You don't
wanna be flying around in circles.

06:32.597 --> 06:36.033
It's fine. Listen, there's something
I need to get off my chest.

06:36.201 --> 06:39.466
If you don't see a doctor soon,
it'll be your earlobe.

06:39.671 --> 06:42.231
- Are you gonna listen or what?
- Sorry. I'm all ears.

06:42.407 --> 06:43.999
No, wait, that's you.

06:44.843 --> 06:48.142
- You know what, forget about it.
- No, no, no. Come on. Talk to me.

06:48.413 --> 06:51.075
- It's about the girl I'm dating.
- Berta's daughter.

06:51.616 --> 06:52.810
How did you know?

06:54.452 --> 06:58.718
Your idiot son doesn't have a single tell,
but you I can read like a stop sign.

06:59.958 --> 07:02.984
Okay. I was gonna build up
to a big reveal, but...

07:03.161 --> 07:04.890
Just cut to the chase.

07:06.131 --> 07:09.328
You remember how I had a little crush on
Naomi when she was pregnant?

07:09.501 --> 07:13.494
A little crush? You were like
a monkey trying to hump a watermelon.

07:14.005 --> 07:17.133
- Are you gonna let me tell the story?
- I'm just fact-checking.

07:17.308 --> 07:20.937
- Go ahead.
- Anyway, after she had the baby...

07:21.112 --> 07:23.808
...we stayed in touch
and I got to know her and the baby...

07:23.982 --> 07:26.382
...and I'm starting to care about
both of them.

07:26.551 --> 07:29.520
Oh, buddy, you got a heart
as big as your ear.

07:32.090 --> 07:34.490
But you're falling
into the same trap you always do.

07:34.659 --> 07:37.628
- What's that?
- You're a pathological rescuer.

07:37.795 --> 07:41.060
Ever since you were a kid,
bringing home that stray three-legged cat.

07:41.399 --> 07:43.629
Oh, yeah, Tippy.

07:43.801 --> 07:47.965
Finding the sick baby bird, feeding it with
an eyedropper, nursing it back to health.

07:48.139 --> 07:50.471
Until Tippy ate it.

07:50.942 --> 07:52.876
And it's the same thing with women.

07:53.044 --> 07:56.536
You constantly seek out these damaged,
needy broads.

07:57.048 --> 07:58.481
You know, you're right.

07:58.650 --> 08:02.279
Maybe subconsciously, I'm hoping that
if I save them, they'll love me.

08:02.453 --> 08:06.389
Perhaps. Or subconsciously, you realize
the only way an emotionally healthy...

08:06.558 --> 08:10.517
...self-supporting woman would
pick you up is on a scavenger hunt.

08:11.162 --> 08:13.687
But we digress.

08:13.865 --> 08:16.732
Please, continue
with your star-crossed love story.

08:16.901 --> 08:20.200
Well, Naomi and I have been
sneaking around behind Berta's back...

08:20.371 --> 08:22.498
...and I'm starting to feel guilty about it.

08:22.774 --> 08:23.866
You want my advice?

08:24.042 --> 08:28.069
Live with the guilt and see a doctor
before that thing grows teeth.

08:28.580 --> 08:31.276
Don't you think the honorable thing
would be to tell Berta?

08:31.449 --> 08:34.418
Sure, honorable is one way to go.
But may I remind you...

08:34.586 --> 08:38.044
...that this is a woman who's been known
to lift the stove with one hand...

08:38.223 --> 08:40.987
...in order to beat a mouse to death
with the other.

08:43.328 --> 08:45.819
How much honor you think
that little fella had?

08:45.997 --> 08:50.263
Oh, well, now you're being silly. I mean,
Berta's not gonna physically assault me.

08:50.835 --> 08:52.427
I hope you're right.

08:53.771 --> 08:56.205
I've grown to enjoy these little talks.

09:01.512 --> 09:04.037
Why don't you just pay me
what you owe me?

09:04.616 --> 09:06.208
I don't owe you till we're done.

09:07.652 --> 09:09.176
Now throw the dice.

09:12.624 --> 09:14.319
Oh, you just suck.

09:16.194 --> 09:18.560
I wouldn't need a job if
I joined the Army.

09:18.730 --> 09:20.960
- You can't join the Army.
NAoMl: Why not?

09:21.332 --> 09:24.392
Because you already are
all that you can be.

09:24.569 --> 09:26.696
You remember my little burden, Naomi?

09:27.772 --> 09:30.138
Oh, sure, I remember her. Hi.

09:30.642 --> 09:34.043
She's got job interviews this afternoon.
I'm gonna watch the baby.

09:34.212 --> 09:36.077
How are you gonna work
and watch the baby?

09:36.247 --> 09:37.805
Who said I was gonna work?

09:39.851 --> 09:42.411
Hey, Alan. Look who's here.

09:44.355 --> 09:46.346
- Oh, hello.
- Hi.

09:46.524 --> 09:49.254
- Um, Nancy, right?
- Uh, Naomi.

09:49.427 --> 09:51.122
Naomi. Naomi, sure. Ha.

09:51.296 --> 09:53.821
- Been a long time.
- Sure has.

09:53.998 --> 09:57.559
- This must be your baby. Oh, isn't she cute.
- Oh, thanks.

09:57.735 --> 09:59.396
And there's the proud grandma.

09:59.971 --> 10:02.303
Look at her beaming.

10:02.473 --> 10:05.738
Well, dip me in butter
and roll me in nuts.

10:07.378 --> 10:09.539
I, too, am shocked.

10:11.015 --> 10:13.950
So you're the sleazeball
she's been running around with.

10:14.118 --> 10:16.518
Oh, Alan, how could you?

10:16.988 --> 10:19.456
No, it's my fault, Mom.
Alan wanted to tell you.

10:19.624 --> 10:24.061
No, no, it's my responsibility.
If you're gonna do anything, do it to me.

10:30.535 --> 10:32.059
Welcome to the family!

10:40.611 --> 10:43.910
Rise and shine, sleepyhead.

10:45.083 --> 10:46.448
I made you breakfast.

10:47.719 --> 10:50.415
- Really?
- Need to have your morning tinkle first?

10:52.357 --> 10:53.824
No, I'm okay.

10:54.359 --> 10:56.350
Good. I made all your favorites.

10:56.527 --> 11:01.760
Scrambled egg whites, turkey bacon,
rye toast, no butter, decaf coffee.

11:01.933 --> 11:03.264
Well, thank you.

11:03.434 --> 11:07.666
You eat like a 90-year-old man
with stomach cancer, but I don't judge.

11:09.340 --> 11:12.468
So, what do you and my little girl
have planned for today?

11:13.111 --> 11:14.976
Maybe a romantic walk on the beach?

11:15.146 --> 11:17.671
A cozy picnic?
I could pack you a lunch.

11:18.082 --> 11:20.448
- Uh, gee, Berta, I don't really...
- or how about this:

11:20.618 --> 11:25.385
I'll watch the baby and the two of you can
spend the afternoon in bed getting sticky.

11:26.591 --> 11:32.291
Well, uh, as lovely as that sounds, I wasrt
really planning on seeing Naomi today.

11:32.463 --> 11:36.422
Why not? What's wrong? Oh, please
don't tell me there's something wrong.

11:36.601 --> 11:39.229
I mean, you ain't much,
but you're the best she ever had.

11:40.905 --> 11:44.671
No, no, no. Nothing's wrong.
I just... I have to go to work today.

11:44.842 --> 11:46.002
Oh. Ha, ha.

11:46.177 --> 11:48.145
- Right. Silly me.
- Ah.

11:48.312 --> 11:50.542
Naomi never dated anybody
with a job before.

11:52.250 --> 11:54.480
At least not one that's indoors and legal.

11:55.653 --> 11:56.677
I understand.

11:57.155 --> 11:59.020
Well, you let me know if you need anything.

11:59.190 --> 12:01.351
- I will.
- Ironing? Groceries?

12:01.526 --> 12:03.323
I could lance that ear for you.

12:04.228 --> 12:05.661
Uh, no, thanks.

12:05.830 --> 12:09.857
I know what I'm doing. I spent a summer
castrating sheep in Montana.

12:11.636 --> 12:15.936
- I'll keep that in mind, but I think it's fine.
- Okay.

12:17.608 --> 12:20.338
You made an old lady very happy, Alan.

12:21.746 --> 12:24.579
I'm... glad.

12:27.084 --> 12:28.108
Bye-bye now.

12:29.053 --> 12:30.850
Bye-bye.

12:34.192 --> 12:37.025
Oh, I am so screwed.

12:37.895 --> 12:40.523
- Charlie?
I'm in the bathroom, Alan.

12:41.399 --> 12:44.835
Um, I've got kind of a delicate problem.

12:45.002 --> 12:46.936
The antibiotics are in my dresser drawer.

12:48.639 --> 12:51.039
No, no, it's Berta.
She's being ridiculously nice to me.

12:51.209 --> 12:54.508
I'm afraid what might happen
if I break up with her daughter.

12:54.679 --> 12:57.045
Oh, you can't break up
with her daughter.

12:57.215 --> 12:59.547
What do you mean,
I can't break up with her?

12:59.984 --> 13:02.316
Well, I guess you could, but:

13:04.755 --> 13:08.714
So, what am I supposed to do?
Marry Naomi just to keep Berta happy?

13:08.893 --> 13:12.954
You don't have to marry her, just let
the relationship follow its natural course.

13:13.130 --> 13:14.222
Natural course?

13:14.866 --> 13:19.565
Think about it, Alan. Any woman,
given enough time, will grow to loathe you.

13:22.373 --> 13:24.398
My God, you're right.

13:24.942 --> 13:27.843
So I just have to stick it out with Naomi
until she hates my guts.

13:28.012 --> 13:30.276
How long could it take?

13:30.882 --> 13:34.613
Damn it, Charlie,
get your lazy ass out of that bed.

13:34.785 --> 13:36.753
Hello, bright eyes.

13:37.722 --> 13:40.691
- Hi.
- I bagged you a lunch to take to work.

13:40.858 --> 13:42.519
- No kidding?
- Yeah.

13:42.693 --> 13:44.820
I also tossed in a packet of vitamin E.

13:44.996 --> 13:47.430
Help you chalk up the old pool cue
for Naomi.

13:49.567 --> 13:51.967
- Thanks.
- Come here, give me some sugar.

13:52.136 --> 13:53.433
Mwah.

13:58.976 --> 14:02.036
Oh, you are so screwed.

14:04.749 --> 14:05.807
Here you go.

14:05.983 --> 14:08.645
One hot chocolate
for the lactating mommy.

14:08.819 --> 14:10.218
Thank you.

14:10.388 --> 14:13.323
&lt;i>I see little Brittany Pam
is having the grande boobaccino.&lt;/i>

14:13.491 --> 14:16.927
Yeah, and she's biting the straw.

14:18.296 --> 14:20.355
Listen, you got any plans
for Saturday night?

14:20.531 --> 14:21.793
I don't think so. Why?

14:21.966 --> 14:25.129
Well, my mom wants to have
a big family dinner over at her place.

14:25.870 --> 14:27.735
Family? Uh, whose family?

14:28.372 --> 14:31.671
You know, me, you, Jake, Charlie,
my mom, your mom.

14:31.842 --> 14:32.900
Oh, oh.

14:33.077 --> 14:35.011
Well, uh, that sounds like fun.

14:35.179 --> 14:36.441
- Doesrt it?
- Yeah. Yeah.

14:36.614 --> 14:38.673
Unfortunately, I'm busy this Saturday.

14:38.849 --> 14:41.079
- But you just said...
- I misspoke.

14:41.652 --> 14:44.815
Oh, I get it. I'm not good enough
to meet your mother.

14:44.989 --> 14:48.652
Oh, no, no, no. I'm just...
Uh, I'm concerned about the baby.

14:49.393 --> 14:52.362
- Why?
- Oh, boy. Uh...

14:52.530 --> 14:54.896
...I was hoping
I wouldn't have to tell you this...

14:55.066 --> 15:00.834
...but my mother
feeds on the souls of the young.

15:01.672 --> 15:04.004
- Okay, just forget it.
- Oh, come on, Naomi.

15:04.175 --> 15:07.667
I mean, don't you think a family dinner
is pushing things a little too fast?

15:07.845 --> 15:11.110
Too fast? You werert worried about
going too fast on our first date...

15:11.282 --> 15:13.182
...when you chewed through
my nursing bra.

15:13.351 --> 15:15.876
In my defense,
I didn't know about the flaps.

15:16.787 --> 15:18.516
You know,
I thought that you were different.

15:18.689 --> 15:22.090
I am different. Ask anybody.
They'll tell you, "Alars different. "

15:22.259 --> 15:25.695
No. No, no, you're not.
You're just like all the rest.

15:25.863 --> 15:28.798
&lt;i>Flirtsy, squirtsy and then arrivederci.&lt;/i>

15:29.600 --> 15:32.068
- Naomi, I didn't mean to...
- I'm not that kind of girl anymore.

15:32.236 --> 15:35.364
I am a mama now
and I demand to be treated with respect.

15:35.539 --> 15:37.939
Sweetie, sweetie, calm down.
I do respect you.

15:38.109 --> 15:40.771
I just thought that the dinner
was a little premature.

15:40.945 --> 15:44.574
Premature? You werert worried about
being premature on our first date...

15:44.749 --> 15:46.808
...when you ruined
a perfectly good sweater.

15:46.984 --> 15:50.215
You know what? Saturday's fine.
Dinner sounds great. We'll be there.

15:50.388 --> 15:52.754
Yeah, damn right, you'll be there.

15:53.057 --> 15:56.424
What? You never seen
a screaming woman with a bare boob?

16:01.565 --> 16:04.728
This is just mortifying.

16:04.902 --> 16:07.928
- Mom.
- It's one thing to diddle the help, Alan.

16:08.105 --> 16:11.074
It's another thing to dine with them.

16:11.509 --> 16:13.841
- Jake, are you listening to your iPod?
- No.

16:14.011 --> 16:16.036
Well, start.

16:17.348 --> 16:19.316
Naomi is not the help.

16:19.583 --> 16:24.145
Oh, forgive me.
She's the maid's round-heeled daughter.

16:24.321 --> 16:28.917
I mean, I'd expect this from Charlie.
He'd hump a grilled cheese sandwich.

16:29.694 --> 16:32.686
- Thanks, Mom.
- You're welcome, darling.

16:32.863 --> 16:35.354
And what, pray,
is going on with your ear?

16:35.533 --> 16:36.932
Oh, it's fine.

16:37.201 --> 16:40.068
Looks like a cherry tomato.

16:40.271 --> 16:42.330
His lady friend thinks it's "darn sexy. "

16:44.075 --> 16:49.172
Don't worry. You won't be the only one
at the table tonight with a raging infection.

16:49.346 --> 16:51.473
It's not infected.

16:51.649 --> 16:53.844
It's got a pulse, Alan.

16:54.785 --> 16:57.185
Look, Mom, there is no reason
to look down your nose at Naomi.

16:57.354 --> 17:00.846
She and her mom are decent,
hard-working, salt-of-the-earth people.

17:01.025 --> 17:03.391
Well, pardon me.

17:04.528 --> 17:06.962
You know,
it's tacky to arrive empty-handed.

17:07.131 --> 17:12.330
Perhaps we should stop and pick up a box
of wine or some aerosol cheese.

17:12.503 --> 17:14.801
Oh, Mom, you're on fire tonight.

17:14.972 --> 17:17.497
It's the new meds.
They mix well with liquor.

17:18.676 --> 17:21.201
Oh, this was a bad idea.

17:22.046 --> 17:25.209
Charlie, didn't you tell him
that's the gay ear?

17:36.927 --> 17:38.417
This is nice flatware.

17:38.596 --> 17:41.565
I gave the same pattern to Charlie
for his birthday.

17:41.732 --> 17:43.825
Yeah, he gave it to me.

17:44.001 --> 17:45.832
Next year, he wants a roasting pan.

17:48.405 --> 17:50.270
You gave away my flatware?

17:50.441 --> 17:53.433
To be fair, Mom, I gave it to you.

17:54.612 --> 17:58.514
So, Berta. Nice house.
When do we take the tour?

17:58.682 --> 18:01.082
- Have you been to the can yet?
- Yeah.

18:01.252 --> 18:02.617
You took it.

18:04.054 --> 18:05.453
Okay.

18:07.391 --> 18:08.722
I wanna make a toast.

18:08.893 --> 18:11.259
Oh, good, a reason to drink.

18:11.428 --> 18:13.020
To Naomi and Alan.

18:13.197 --> 18:15.358
Thank God they found each other.

18:15.533 --> 18:17.967
Let's face it,
they were both running out of options.

18:18.502 --> 18:19.901
- Hear, hear.
- Hang on, hang on.

18:20.070 --> 18:23.267
I'd like to propose an addendum
to the toast.

18:23.440 --> 18:25.874
A subordinate clause, if you will.

18:26.043 --> 18:29.342
Uh, while Naomi and I are enjoying
each other's company...

18:29.513 --> 18:32.573
...we are proceeding in a very slow
and cautious manner.

18:33.050 --> 18:34.608
Except when we're having sex.

18:36.287 --> 18:39.415
Time and place, Naomi. Time and place.

18:39.590 --> 18:43.993
Yeah, well, I wish you'd spend a little
more time and aim for the right place.

18:44.795 --> 18:47.730
Oh, God, just kill me now.

18:47.965 --> 18:48.989
- Jake?
- IPod?

18:49.166 --> 18:50.326
Attaboy.

18:51.135 --> 18:53.194
Excuse me. Uh...

18:53.504 --> 18:56.871
I'd like to say a few words
before we fold up the dining-room table...

18:57.041 --> 18:59.566
...and commence the square dancing.

19:00.110 --> 19:03.443
Alan, you're my son and I love you.

19:05.049 --> 19:06.641
But you and I are through.

19:08.419 --> 19:10.512
- What?
- I just can't bear it anymore.

19:10.688 --> 19:12.280
I have to cut you loose.

19:13.357 --> 19:16.292
Is that all it takes?
Hey, Berta, you got any other daughters?

19:18.162 --> 19:19.595
HECToR:
Naomi? Are you in there?

19:20.097 --> 19:22.463
- Hector?
- Go away! Nobody's home!

19:22.900 --> 19:23.924
Mom.

19:24.301 --> 19:28.362
If that loser steps one foot inside
this house, I'm getting out my nail gun.

19:28.906 --> 19:32.137
&lt;i>Oh, wonderful, we're going to be
on an episode of Cops.&lt;/i>

19:34.311 --> 19:36.939
- What are you doing here?
- I've come to see my daughter.

19:37.114 --> 19:38.604
- Is that her?
- What do you care?

19:38.816 --> 19:40.408
- You ran off.
HECToR: I didn't run off.

19:40.618 --> 19:42.449
I couldn't get back across the border.

19:42.620 --> 19:45.180
They're cracking down
because of these damn Arabs.

19:45.356 --> 19:46.983
Oh. Why didn't you call me?

19:47.157 --> 19:50.422
I did call. Didrt your mother
give you my messages?

19:51.295 --> 19:53.627
Whoops.

19:54.365 --> 19:57.698
- Oh, Hector, I've missed you so much. Oh.
- I missed you too.

19:59.803 --> 20:01.794
- Alan.
- Yeah?

20:01.972 --> 20:05.169
Your relationship has run
its natural course.

20:05.943 --> 20:08.707
She doesn't hate me yet.
She's just, like...

20:10.014 --> 20:12.608
A toast to Hector and Naomi.

20:13.284 --> 20:16.185
- May their love last forever.
- Hear, hear.

20:16.787 --> 20:18.152
What's with your ear?

20:19.023 --> 20:20.854
I'm gay.

20:38.809 --> 20:39.867
Berta?

20:40.044 --> 20:43.172
Don't bother me, Charlie,
I had a hard night.

20:44.348 --> 20:46.942
If you're so tired,
why don't you just stay home?

20:47.117 --> 20:48.277
Are you kidding?

20:48.452 --> 20:51.853
Hector invited his entire family over
to see the baby.

20:52.022 --> 20:54.684
It's like the Alamo over there.

20:55.526 --> 20:58.427
Well, for the record,
I didn't get any sleep either.

20:58.595 --> 21:02.793
Halfway home, Alars ear blew up and
we had to take him to the emergency room.

21:03.133 --> 21:06.432
- Is he okay?
- Yeah, they were able to save the lobe...

21:06.603 --> 21:10.937
...but I don't think anyone's gonna call it
the gay ear anymore.

21:11.108 --> 21:12.598
Huh.

21:13.310 --> 21:16.541
Well, sweet dreams.

21:17.681 --> 21:19.171
You too.
